	core/libs/facesengine/detection/opencv-dnn/dnnfacedetectorssd.cpp,
	core/libs/facesengine/detection/opencv-dnn/dnnfacedetectorssd.h,
	core/libs/facesengine/detection/opencv-dnn/dnnfacedetectoryolo.cpp,
	core/libs/facesengine/detection/opencv-dnn/dnnfacedetectoryolo.h,
	core/libs/facesengine/detection/opencvdnnfacedetector.cpp,
	core/libs/facesengine/detection/opencvdnnfacedetector.h,
	core/libs/facesengine/detection/opencvfacedetector.cpp,
	core/libs/facesengine/detection/opencvfacedetector.h,
	core/libs/facesengine/recognition/opencv-dnn/dnndbscan.cpp,
	core/libs/facesengine/recognition/opencv-dnn/dnndbscan.h,
	core/libs/facesengine/recognition/opencv-dnn/dnnfaceextractor.cpp,
	core/libs/facesengine/recognition/opencv-dnn/dnnfaceextractor.h: 
	FaceEngine optimization: remove opencv3 haar cascades. Files are the
	same than official opencv and have been copied here originaly
	because files was missing in Windows install. Historically, this
	rules was generalized to Linux and MAcOS. Now, in case of use
	FaceDetector + Haar Cascades engine, we will use files from openCV
	root dir directly.  FaceDetector : be able to switch from DNN to
	Haar Cascades at compilation time. For the moment the preprocessing
	rules in at top of facedetector.cpp, and DNN is used by default.
	With this change, DNN face detector is also use while parsing single
	image for faces from a QImage or a DImg instance. Previous
	implementation mix both DNN and Haar engines in memory. Now only one
	is used in all cases.

