2019-06-09  Gilles Caulier <caulier.gilles@gmail.com>

	* core/CMakeLists.txt, core/cmake/modules/MacroUtils.cmake,
	core/libs/dplugins/webservices/CMakeLists.txt,
	core/libs/facesengine/CMakeLists.txt,
	core/libs/pgfutils/CMakeLists.txt,
	core/libs/rawengine/CMakeLists.txt: first stage to factoring and
	separate compiler warnings options to disable in goal to limit
	traces generate while compilation. In all cases, Clang >=8 give
	better results than GCC while parsing C++ syntax everywehere and
	reports less false positive than GCC. I recommend to switch to Clang
	to compile whole digiKam. Reports on the console are more human
	readable and canbe really considerate has true positive. The Clang
	-Wpedantic for ex, report real problem on C++ syntax. In oppposite,
	GCC -Wpedantic, report plenty false positive with qCdebug which
	transform compilation traces as a mess...

