2018-09-13  Gilles Caulier <caulier.gilles@gmail.com>

	* core/libs/album/albummanager.cpp: fix cppcheck warning about non
	explicit constructor.  Maik, this fix is important, as depending of
	internal compiler rules, the PAlbumPath constructor used to handle
	the one argument PAlbum* can be confused with the constructor taken
	an albumid instead, even if this one take 2 arguments. The proff is
	all error generated by GCC when i introduced the explicit keyword on
	front of this one argument constructor. In fact, GCC is lost to take
	the right constructor when when host PAlbumPath to the QHash table,
	epecially with [] operator. I don't think the previous code is
	bugous as well, but depending of the compiler version the
	constructor binary code can be a garbage and introduce crash in
	specific conditions. In all cases, i think this code will be more
	robust in time.  CCMAIL: metzpinguin@gmail.com

