	utilities/mediaserver/upnpsdk/Platinum/ThirdParty/log4net/log4net.d
	ll,
	utilities/mediaserver/upnpsdk/Platinum/ThirdParty/log4net/log4net.x
	ml, utilities/mediaserver/upnpsdk/README: digiKam DLNA Media Server
	: Important changes here...  The old implementation written by
	student while this summer 2017 do not work. This one based on HUpnp
	library is full of bugs and give multiple unpredictable dysfunctions
	with media render devices. These states was reported to current
	Hupnp maintainer from Github fork project, where library code was
	taken, but maintainer report that he has no time to hack the media
	server part of Hupnp.  So, after to lost more than 3 weeks to hack
	and try to solve myself all issues from Hupnp, i can said "basta"!
	We need another solution to create quickly a DLNA media server into
	digiKam.  The solution come from with Kodi source code (older XBMC
	media manager) which have all the DLNA/UPNP features included since
	a while. Kody use Platinum open source Upnp SDK inside, with a lots
	of patches to improve the DLNA features. Magically this one work
	perfectly with all render devices.  After to hack the complex Kody
	delegate DLNA server implementation while one week, i must admit
	that Platinum SDK is a little bit complex to understand, in goal to
	write quickly a media server with digiKam virtual albums support.
	The solution come from the files media server test implementation
	provided with Platinum SDK which have been adjusted and partially
	re-written for digiKam.  The result is a media server, working
	exactly as previous implementation based Hupnp library and ready to
	use for next 5.8.0 release.  TODO : - These implementations was not
	yet tested under MacOS and Windows. - Platinum source code can be
	certainly cleaned as a lots of parts are not used here (as Scons
	build system for ex.). - More CLI test tools provided by Platinum
	can be compiled with digiKam, as the famous original files media
	server for ex.  Note : the older implementation of digiKam Media
	Server based on Hupnp is saved in dedicated branch
	"developement/hupnp", in case of.  CCMAIL: digikam-devel@kde.org

