2013-04-22  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* libs/database/collectionscanner.cpp,
	libs/database/collectionscanner.h,
	libs/database/collectionscannerhints.cpp,
	libs/database/collectionscannerhints.h,
	libs/database/imagescanner.cpp: Implement reuse of thumbnails by
	hint, and optimize loading of hints.  1) By giving a hint prior to
	and after editing a file where the edit only involved    the
	metadata, with no scan needed, the scan is reduced accordingly.
	The thumbnail in the thumb db (which would usually be regenerated
	due to new    hash, file size, mod time) is reused for the new
	parameters. 2) CollectionScanner objects are created on the stack,
	hints are kept for a longer    time by ScanController. Recording the
	hints by a scanner is not a shallow copy.    Optimize this by
	providing a long-living and thread-safe container object    which
	performs all processing of hints internally while being reused for
	all scanners.

