	Use QScopedArrayPointer for loading image data

2012-01-29  Andi Clemens <andi.clemens@googlemail.com>

	* libs/dimg/loaders/tiffloader.cpp: Use QScopedArrayPointer here, to
	avoid memory issues.  We are using a third party library for loading
	TIFF files. If an exception is thrown or anything else happens so
	that the loading method is exited in an unusual way, the "delete"
	statements will never be executed. Since we can not know when the
	method will exit exactly, a ScopedArrayPointer is the safest way. In
	general we should never call "delete" manually if not absolutely
	necessary, let the compiler / runtime handle this.

