2011-12-21  Andi Clemens <andi.clemens@googlemail.com>

	* libs/dimg/filters/dimgfiltermanager.cpp: fix memory leak:
	DImgFilterGenerator objects are not deleted properly  We save the
	DImgFilterGenerator objects in the filterMap and coreGenerators, but
	we only cleanup coreGenerators in the destructor. This results in a
	memory leak. We can not simply delete the filterMap, because the
	DImgFilterGenerator pointers are shared and therefore the
	application will crash due to multiple delete calls. Use a
	QSharedPointer to avoid the problem.  A new method
	addGenerator(const ImgFilterPtr& generator) has been added to the
	private class, so the code is still API compatible.

