2011-11-07  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* CMakeLists.txt, digikam/CMakeLists.txt,
	digikam/album/albummanager.cpp, digikam/album/albummanager.h,
	digikam/album/albumwatch.cpp, digikam/album/albumwatch.h,
	libs/3rdparty/kinotify/kinotify.cpp,
	libs/3rdparty/kinotify/kinotify.h: On Linux, use Inotify directly
	for file notification changes  Use Sebastian Trueg's KInotify
	wrapper, if Inotify is available. This gives much more detailed
	reports and especially info when a file has been closed after write.
	For a detailed explanation, see

	http://trueg.wordpress.com/2011/10/13/taking-a-break-from-crash-fixing-for-usability/ Separate the file watch code from AlbumManager to a new class, AlbumWatch. Do not watch directories recursively (convenient API, but often inefficient implementation out of our reach). We scan the directories anyway, it is possible and efficient to add each directory = album separately. If Inotify is not available (non-linux), the previous code based on KDirWatch and KIO is still used.  CCMAIL: digikam-devel@kde.org

