2011-10-24  Andi Clemens <andi.clemens@googlemail.com>

	* utilities/advancedrename/parser/modifiers/casemodifier.cpp: Fix
	crash. I had replaced all direct access methods (e.g. bla[0]) with
	const method access (e.g. bla.at(0)) 2 months ago. Unfortunately, I
	have always compiled digiKam with relwithdebinfo, so that I haven't
	seen the Q_ASSERT in action that now occurred when running the unit
	tests. Compiling with debugfull triggered the assert and showed the
	problem that is now fixed with this commit. This shows again that we
	should never use (bla[0]) for access, but the const method
	(bla.at(0)) to find out-of-bound exceptions quickly. But we need to
	make sure to compile with "debugfull" in the development phase, and
	use "relwithdebinfo" before releasing digiKam, since this target
	produces different error and compile messages.

