2011-10-17  Andi Clemens <andi.clemens@googlemail.com>

	* libs/dmetadata/dmetadata.cpp: The last commit broke compilation
	because a "break" was added to the MetadataInfo::Orientation case.
	The problem is that if no value is matched inside the switch, we do
	not return a value for the orientation.  But the bigger problem is
	that before the "break" statement we would have fallen through to
	the MetadataInfo::Make case statement, which is totally wrong in
	this case.  So please do not ignore compile warnings, they are there
	for a reason :-) Always add "break" statements, even in the default
	handling. If a fall-through is valid, add a comment to the source
	code to make the situation clear to other coders.

2011-10-17  Andi Clemens <andi.clemens@googlemail.com>

	* libs/models/imagesortsettings.cpp: add comment about possible
	fal-through, otherwise add a break here

