2010-12-06  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* libs/models/categorizeditemmodel.cpp,
	libs/models/categorizeditemmodel.h: Two generic models:
	CategorizedItemModel is a convenience class around
	QStandardItemModel supporting categorization. ActionItemModel allows
	to access QActions through a model: The actions' text, icon and
	state is mapped to the model's indices, and slots allow to map
	actions on an index in a view (like activate()) to an action's
	signals (like triggered()). The model supports recursive listing of
	a widget's actions and menus and filtering through a whitelist, so
	you can give the menuBar() to the model.   svn
	path=/branches/extragear/graphics/digikam/; revision=1204258

