2010-11-25  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* libs/versionmanager/versionmanager.cpp,
	libs/versionmanager/versionmanager.h: Extend the version manager,
	giving it the power to make the decisions when saving a versioned
	image.  - the VersionNamingScheme is an interface to implement the
	naming   scheme of saved files.   Implemented is only the current
	"_v....jpg" scheme with some   adjustments to reduce dimensionality
	(editing v3 -> v3v1? No, v4) - VersionManagerSettings is a container
	for relevant settings.   Still some TODO here. -
	VersionFileOperation is a structure giving the result from the
	VersionManager:   it can tell where to save which files and versions
	- the VersionManager itself is no longer a singleton, but a normal
	class where some virtual methods can be overridden.   ImageWindow
	will have such a class, and give it the settings from AlbumSettings
	svn path=/branches/extragear/graphics/digikam/; revision=1200708

2010-11-25  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* libs/database/collectionscanner.cpp,
	libs/database/collectionscanner.h,
	libs/database/databaseconstants.cpp,
	libs/database/databaseconstants.h, libs/database/imagescanner.cpp,
	libs/database/imagescanner.h: Fully implement scanning of the image
	history. The process is now done in three stages: 1) The UUID and
	history is read from metadata and stored in the database.    If
	there is history (new file) or the UUID changed (modified file),
	the image is marked for stage two 2) After all images are scanned:
	The history from the database is read,    all history image ids
	resolved to entries in the database.    The relation cloud (image
	relations table) is filled from the    transitive closure of the
	resulting graph.    The cloud is marked for stage 3. 3) The full
	"relations cloud" is read into a graph.    Entries are categorized
	and tagged as Original, Current or Intermediate.  svn
	path=/branches/extragear/graphics/digikam/; revision=1200705

