	* libs/dimg/filters/fx/filmgrainfilter.cpp,
	libs/dimg/filters/fx/raindropfilter.cpp: Port FilmGrainFilter to
	RandomNumberGenerator.  Please check these changes:  1)
	d->generator.seed(1); // noise will always be the same  As before,
	the generator is initialized with a constant seed. We could just as
	well initialize with a random seed.  2)  -    return
	((double)(qrand() % (int)range) - range/2.0) ; +    return
	d->generator.number(- range/2, range/2);  Before, the
	randomizeUniform returned random values in steps of 1 (cast to int),
	e.g., if range was 5, (-2.5, -1.5, -0.5, 0.5, 1.5, 2.5). The method
	name promises a uniform distribution (any value in [-2.5, 2.5]), and
	that's what it's now doing.   svn
