2010-11-03  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* libs/dimg/filters/randomnumbergenerator.cpp,
	libs/dimg/filters/randomnumbergenerator.h: Adding an implementation
	of a deterministic random number generator based on Boost Random,
	using the MT19937 Mersenne twister as engine. Adding a second class
	which provides access to a non- deterministic random generator, for
	Linux, /dev/urandom (for Windows, using a workaround)  Why?
	qsrand/qrand do not guarantee the algorithm across platforms. Using
	the boost implementation should allow us to replay a filter just by
	storing the random seed.  The non-deterministic generator is on
	Linux the best choice to generate image UUIDs. With QUuid, I saw
	repeatable ids.   svn path=/branches/extragear/graphics/digikam/;
	revision=1192650

