2010-10-13  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* libs/database/databasebackend_p.h,
	libs/database/databasecorebackend.cpp,
	libs/database/databasecorebackend.h,
	libs/database/databasecorebackend_p.h: - change handling of a locked
	SQLite database   This situation is actually not an error, but a
	common collision.   The Qt driver per default waits for 5s, remove
	this and to our own waiting.   In any case, waiting is fine grained
	at 10ms (this may be a bit short).   While waiting, free the
	DatabaseAccess lock. Waiting threads will   be woken when a
	transaction finishes (a transaction without DatabaseAccess   lock is
	the common case for in-process locked file) - enable the shared
	cache of SQLite. Experimentally, but I dont see   why it shouldnt
	work - when starting or committing a transaction, also do error
	handling,   in particular for SQLite locked file  svn
	path=/branches/extragear/graphics/digikam/; revision=1185472

2010-10-13  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* libs/threads/threadmanager.cpp, libs/threads/workerobject.cpp,
	libs/threads/workerobject.h: Fix three major bugs in WorkerObject  -
	QThread::quit shall be used only with QThread::exec.   Using
	EventLoop::exec doesn't work with QThread::quit.   (works only the
	first time). Because QThread::exec is protected   for unknown
	reasons, we must exec and quit the event loop directly. - after
	transitionToInactive, the object was subject to deletion,   so
	parkObject unsafe. By informing the object of the runnable,   we
	prevent this crash - in moveToCurrentThread, wait until the object
	is really moved to destination thread - make connectAndSchedule work
	properly   svn path=/branches/extragear/graphics/digikam/;
	revision=1185469

