2010-09-11  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* libs/dimg/dimg.h, libs/dimg/dimgscale.cpp: Add a new scaling
	method: DImg::smoothScaleClipped This method can be used when only a
	section of a scaled image shall be repainted. smoothScaleSection()
	wants to have a _source_ region, but when repainting, we need to
	specify a _destination_ region. There is often no corresponding
	source region in integer coordinates for a dest region in integer
	coordinates!  Example: A 3x3 image   0  50  75 100 150 175 200 250
	255  scaled to 2x2:  49  89 183 224  Now I want to repaint pixel
	(1,1), 224. The correct source region is (1.5, 1.5; 1.5x1.5).  This
	pixel value is (255 + 1/2*250 + 1/2*175 + 1/4*150)/(1 + 1/2 + 1/2 +
	1/4). smoothScaleSection(1, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1) will give me (255 + 250 +
	175 + 150)/4, which is different.  With smoothScaleClipped(2, 2, 1,
	1, 1, 1), I will get 224!   svn
	path=/branches/extragear/graphics/digikam/; revision=1174246

