2010-09-07  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* CMakeLists.txt, utilities/facedetection/facepipeline.cpp,
	utilities/facedetection/facepipeline.h,
	utilities/facedetection/facepipeline_p.h: Add a new class
	"FacePipeline" which implements an extensively multithreaded face
	detection process based on the metaphor of a pipeline.  The
	individual parts in the pipeline can be plugged as needed.
	Specifically, there is - ScanStateFilter, a DynamicThread with a
	traditional mutex-protected task queue,   to implement rescan from
	scratch / continue (TODO: remove unconfirmed entries   prior to
	rescan) - PreviewLoader, a PreviewLoadThread - DetectionWorker,
	doing the face detection. Multithreading is based on the
	WorkerObject paradigm (object moved to thread, interthread signals)
	- with the help of a ParallelPipes element, multiple detectors can
	be   plugged in parallel. If you have a double core, you will get
	two. - RecognitionWorker, for face recognition, based on
	RecognitionDatabase.   Needs testing. - DatabaseWriter: finally,
	this one is not multithread. Can be done though ;-)   Simply uses a
	FaceIface to write to db.  It works pretty well for me, giving full
	100% on both cores and thus much much faster than before. A lot of
	new code though.   svn path=/branches/extragear/graphics/digikam/;
	revision=1172650

