2010-07-30  Aditya Jitesh Bhatt <adityabhatt1991@gmail.com>

	* utilities/batch/batchfacedetector.cpp: Fixed bug from previous
	commit. In this one, I create a new tag "/Scanned/Faces", which is
	for all images that have been scanned for Faces so far. This is
	easier than creating my own table matching image urls to a
	scanned/not scanned value. Possibly this can be useful for other
	batch jobs in the future too, maybe each batch job can create their
	own tag under the "/Scanned" tag. For ex, if there is a batch job
	that fixes red eyes from detected faces in the collection, it could
	have it's own tag, such as "/Scanned/Redeye". The tags under
	"Scanned" could be barred from being written to the metadata, or
	possibly from even being shown to the user. CCMAIL:
	marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de  svn
