2009-11-22  Andrew Coles <andrew.i.coles@googlemail.com>

	* utilities/queuemanager/basetools/enhance/noisereduction.cpp: 
	Proof-reading:  - photographs noise -> photograph noise.  It either
	needs an apostrophe (i.e. photographs' noise), in which case
	photographs' is an adjective describing noise; or to be written as
	'photograph noise', a compound noun.  I went for the latter, as it's
	more common idiomatic usage.  - NoiseReduction -> Noise Reduction.
	English is far more reluctant than German to make one-word
	über-nouns.  - 'denoising of the image' -> 'denoising the image'.
	As with 'driving the car', &c.  The other solution, retaining the
	of, is to add 'the' before it, i.e. 'the denoising of the image' -
	closer to other languages, but not idiomatic English.  Bien
	cordialement,  Andrew   svn path=/trunk/extragear/graphics/digikam/;
	revision=1052766

