2009-11-04  Andi Clemens <andi.clemens@gmx.net>

	* libs/dimg/dimg.cpp: Little speed gain: if (under) / if (over)
	calls in a for-loop are expensive, if we don't need to check for
	this all the time, we should avoid it. Sure this will blow up the
	code (and duplicate it), but it saves computation time. On my
	machine I got a 22% speed gain. The only bottleneck left in this
	method is the check for black / white color for each pixel. Any idea
	how to make this faster? Right now these checks make 60% of the
	computation time in the for-loop (e.g. dimg.cpp:1602)
	CCMAIL:digikam-devel@kde.org  svn
	path=/trunk/extragear/graphics/digikam/; revision=1044664

