2009-08-01  Marcel Wiesweg <marcel.wiesweg@gmx.de>

	* NEWS, libs/dimg/loaders/tiffloader.cpp: If the image does not have
	alpha, we must not set TIFFTAG_EXTRASAMPLES at all. If setting
	UNASSOC_ALPHA, libtiff assumes the last value for a pixel is a mask.
	When settings samples_per_pixel to three, there are 3-1=2 color
	channels left which libtiff (and noone really) cannot handle.  BUG:
	201746  svn path=/trunk/extragear/graphics/digikam/;
	revision=1005615

