	* libs/database/databasebackend.cpp: Call databaseForThread before
	touching the transaction count. If the very first thing that a
	thread did in its life was creating a transaction, the database
	connection would be opened just after incrementTransactionCount(),
	and open() would reset the transaction counter from 1 to 0, so that
	all subsequent transaction would not be committed. (This was the
	case first time with the MetadataManager worker threads assigning
	rating, which seemed to work because the ImageInfo was updated, but
	not the database)  svn path=/trunk/extragear/graphics/digikam/;
	revision=974514

