	* digikam/albumiconitem.cpp, digikam/albumiconview.cpp,
	digikam/albumiconview.h: With my test generateFuzzyPixmap()
	accounted for 55% of the CPU cost of icon view item drawing. We
	cannot simply cache one pixmap here because every thumbnail can have
	different width or height (either is the thumbnail size, the other
	depends on the aspect ratio). We can take care for the majority of
	use cases though where the aspect ratios are limited, you usually
	have an album of one camera only with landscape/portrait. Cache the
	last 10 used fuzzy pixmaps in a central place in AlbumIconView. For
	albums with identical aspect ratios this eliminates CPU usage for
	fuzzyRect generation.  svn path=/trunk/extragear/graphics/digikam/;
	revision=896901

