2008-07-25  Andi Clemens <andi.clemens@gmx.net>

	* libs/widgets/common/thumbbar.cpp, libs/widgets/common/thumbbar.h: 
	Images get removed twice from the thumbbar view when removing them
	via keyboard shortcut or context menu. This happened due to the use
	of the ThumbBarView::removeItem() method in the appropriate slot as
	well as in the destructor of a ThumbBarItem. To obtain backward
	compatibility we move the context of removeItem() into a new method
	takeItem() and call this new method from within the destructor of a
	ThumbBarItem, removeItem only calls delete now. This way we can
	remove an item "the old way" but also by calling just delete.
	Somehow the KDE3 branch is not affected by this because the
	destructor is never called at all (I don't know why).  CCBUGS:166440
	svn path=/trunk/extragear/graphics/digikam/; revision=837619

