	* libs/database/databasebackend.cpp,
	libs/database/databasebackend.h: Use the Qt4 SQL module with the
	sqlite3 driver as the SQL backend, remove old code accessing
	libsqlite3 directly.  The switch is long planned. There are no major
	code changes, the database backend provides mostly a drop-in
	replacement for the old API. It gives us a clean and complete Qt
	API, and I want to use prepared query to try to speed up some batch
	operations. If we decide in the future that we want to support
	MySQL, here we have the support for free by Qt.  CCMAIL:
