2007-03-16  Gilles Caulier <caulier.gilles@gmail.com>

	* imageplugins/common/Makefile.am,
	imageplugins/common/cimgiface/CImg.h,
	imageplugins/common/cimgiface/LICENSE.txt,
	imageplugins/common/cimgiface/Makefile.am,
	imageplugins/common/cimgiface/cimgiface.cpp,
	imageplugins/common/cimgiface/cimgiface.h: digikam from trunk :  -
	Bye bye to old Cimg library interface.  - Welcome to the new
	GreyCRestoration interface, more fast, more easy to use, more easy
	to maintain, more easy to update.  Note : The new
	CImg::Greycstoration algorithm is able to use multiprocessors! It
	use a parallelized computation interface to optimize performances.
	Actually the computation code is forked into 2 seperate threads if
	you have 2 processors (for example with dual-core cpu).  In the
	future, the GreyCStoration algorithm and the CImg library will be
	able to detect the number of CPU available and fork with the
	appropriate threads number accordinly.  CCMAIL:
	digikam-devel@kde.org  svn
	path=/trunk/extragear/graphics/digikamimageplugins/; revision=643046


