	imageplugins/hotpixels/hotpixelfixer.cpp,
	imageplugins/hotpixels/hotpixelfixer.h,
	imageplugins/hotpixels/imageeffect_hotpixels.cpp,
	imageplugins/hotpixels/imageeffect_hotpixels.h: digiKam Hot Pixels
	Tool :  - Polish code : never use tabs in source code. This way
	breaking print issue. - Always using current plugin namespace in all
	source code (excepted imageplugin class) to prevent memory problems
	with others plugins ! - No need to include class file in header if
	you use pointers. Just declare "class Foo;" instead. This way
	decrease compilation duration. - Always separate data and methods in
	header file to increase code visibility.  Unai, you can take a look
	in the Qt3 coding style, explained in this book :
	http://digikam3rdparty.free.fr/Books/C++programingwithQT3.pdf
	CCMAIL: ugarro@telefonica.net  svn
