2005-06-09  Renchi Raju <renchi.raju@kdemail.net>

	* digikam/digikam/albumfolderview.cpp,
	digikam/digikam/albumfolderview.h: * don't store AlbumFolderViewItem
	in a dict with albumID as key. If an Album is moved to a new place,
	first an album created signal will be fired and then an album
	deleted signal will be fired. Since both albums will have the same
	id, you will end up deleting the viewitem for the new album and
	leave a dangling pointer for the old album. Make use of
	Album::setExtraData() and Album::extraData() *
	AlbumManager::createPAlbum() returns a pointer to the new created
	Album if successful. Use it directly instead of connecting to a
	slot. All of this is documented.  CCMAIL: joern.ahrens@kdemail.net
	svn path=/branches/digikam/0.8-experimental/; revision=423873

