2005-02-28  Gilles Caulier <caulier.gilles@gmail.com>

	* imageplugins/distortionfx/Makefile.am,
	imageplugins/distortionfx/digikamimageplugin_distortionfx.desktop,
	imageplugins/distortionfx/digikamimageplugin_distortionfx_ui.rc,
	imageplugins/distortionfx/hi32-action-distortionfx.png,
	imageplugins/distortionfx/imageeffect_distortionfx.cpp,
	imageplugins/distortionfx/imageeffect_distortionfx.h,
	imageplugins/distortionfx/imageplugin_distortionfx.cpp,
	imageplugins/distortionfx/imageplugin_distortionfx.h: New digiKam
	image editor plugin : Distortion FX.  With this plugin you can apply
	distortion special effects to a photograph. Current effects are
	available :  - Mosaic: divides the photograph into rectangular cells
	and then recreates it by filling those cells with average pixel
	value.  - Fish Eyes: Warps the photograph around a 3D spherical
	shape to reproduce the common photograh 'fish eyes' effect.  -
	Twirl: spins the photograph to produce a swirl pattern.  -
	Cilindrical: warps the photograph around a cylinder.  - Caricature:
	Fish Eyes effect inverted.  - Multiple Corners: splits the
	photograph like a 'Multiple Corners' pattern.  - Waves Horizontal:
	distorts the photograph with horizontal waves.  - Waves Vertical:
	distorts the photograph with verticals waves.  - Block Waves 1:
	divides the image into cells and makes it look as if it is being
	viewed through glass blocks.  - Block Waves 2: like Block Waves 1
	but with another version of glass blocks distorsion.  - Circular
	Waves 1: distorts the photograph with circular waves.  - Circular
	Waves 2: other variation of Circular Waves effect.  - Polar
	Coordinates: converts the photograph from rectangular to polar
	coordinates .  - Unpolar Coordinates: Polar Coordinate effect
	inverted.  - Tile: splits the photograph into square blocks and move
	them randomly inside the image.  A screenshot is available at this
	url :
	http://extragear.kde.org/apps/digikamimageplugins/distortionfx.png
	CCMAIL: digikam-devel@lists.sourceforge.net  svn
	path=/trunk/kdeextragear-3/digikamimageplugins/; revision=393823

2005-02-28  Gilles Caulier <caulier.gilles@gmail.com>

	* imageplugins/blurfx/Makefile.am,
	imageplugins/blurfx/digikamimageplugin_blurfx.desktop,
	imageplugins/blurfx/digikamimageplugin_blurfx_ui.rc,
	imageplugins/blurfx/hi32-action-blurfx.png,
	imageplugins/blurfx/imageeffect_blurfx.cpp,
	imageplugins/blurfx/imageeffect_blurfx.h,
	imageplugins/blurfx/imageplugin_blurfx.cpp,
	imageplugins/blurfx/imageplugin_blurfx.h: New digiKam image editor
	plugin : Blur FX.  With this plugin you can apply blurring special
	effects to a photograph. Current effects are available :  - Zoom
	Blur:  blurs the image along radial lines starting from a specified
	center point. This simulates the blur of a zooming camera.  - Radial
	Blur: blurs the image by rotating the pixels around the specified
	center point. This simulates the blur of a rotating camera.  - Far
	Blur: blurs the image by using far pixels. This simulates the blur
	of an unfocalized camera lens.  - Motion Blur: blurs the image by
	moving the pixels horizontally. This simulates the blur of a moving
	camera.  - Skake Blur: blurs the image by skaking randomly the
	pixels. This simulates the blur of a random moving camera.  -
	Softner Blur: blurs the image softly in dark tones and hardly in
	light tones. This gives images a dreamy and glossy soft focus
	effect. It's ideal for creating ro:mantic portraits, glamour
	photographs, or giving images a warm and subtle glow.  - Frost
	Glass: blurs the image by randomly disperse light coming through a
	frosted glass.  A screenshot is available at this url :
	http://extragear.kde.org/apps/digikamimageplugins/blurfx.png
	CCMAIL: digikam-devel@lists.sourceforge.net  svn
	path=/trunk/kdeextragear-3/digikamimageplugins/; revision=393822

